.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt DMA_INFO 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm dma_info
.Nd describe a DMA buffer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fn dma_info h out
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm fills the
.Em DmaInfo
record
.Sy { bus_addr: u64, len: u64, flags: u32, _pad: u32 }
for the DMA buffer handle
.Fa h :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fa bus_addr
The bus address of the first byte (physical address plus the device domain's
offset; the identity domain has offset 0).
.It Fa len
The allocation length in bytes.
.It Fa flags
Bit 0
.Dv UNPROTECTED :
set on every buffer while no IOMMU domain protects the device (always,
today).  The kernel never claims DMA isolation.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EBADF
.Fa h
is not a DMA buffer handle.
.It Er EACCES
The handle lacks the
.Dv READ
right.
.It Er EFAULT
.Fa out
is not writable user memory.
.El
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
